stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  accTitle: UCP checkout session status (v2026-08-25), with the AP2 lock
  accDescr: State diagram: UCP checkout session status (v2026-08-25), with the AP2 lock. 6 states: incomplete, requires_escalation, ready_for_complete, complete_in_progress, completed, and canceled. Starts in incomplete. Ends in completed and canceled. 13 transitions. From incomplete to ready_for_complete when All information collected, no Action outstanding (PUT /checkout-sessions/ id (update_checkout)). From incomplete to requires_escalation when Business needs data its API cannot collect, or a policy needs buyer review (POST or PUT /checkout-sessions response). From requires_escalation to incomplete when Issue resolved through an update (PUT /checkout-sessions/ id ). From requires_escalation to completed when Buyer finishes on the business UI through continue_url (continue_url (browser), then GET /checkout-sessions/ id ). From ready_for_complete to completed when Complete Checkout succeeds synchronously (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /complete (complete_checkout)). From ready_for_complete to complete_in_progress when Complete Checkout accepted for asynchronous processing (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /complete). From ready_for_complete to incomplete when Complete returns a recoverable change (for example payment_failed or out_of_stock) (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /complete). From ready_for_complete to requires_escalation when Complete returns a buyer handoff (requires_buyer_input or requires_buyer_review) (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /complete). From complete_in_progress to completed when Business finishes processing any Action resolved (GET /checkout-sessions/ id (get_checkout)). From incomplete to canceled when Platform cancels, or the session expires (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /cancel (cancel_checkout)). From requires_escalation to canceled when Platform cancels, or the session expires (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /cancel). From ready_for_complete to canceled when Platform cancels, or the session expires (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /cancel). From complete_in_progress to canceled when Session invalid or expired (cancellation race rules apply) (POST /checkout-sessions/ id /cancel).
  state "incomplete" as s_incomplete
  state "requires_escalation" as s_requires_escalation
  state "ready_for_complete" as s_ready_for_complete
  state "complete_in_progress" as s_complete_in_progress
  state "completed" as s_completed
  state "canceled" as s_canceled
  [*] --> s_incomplete
  s_incomplete --> s_ready_for_complete : All information collected, no Action outstanding
  s_incomplete --> s_requires_escalation : Business needs data its API cannot collect, or a policy needs buyer review
  s_requires_escalation --> s_incomplete : Issue resolved through an update
  s_requires_escalation --> s_completed : Buyer finishes on the business UI through continue_url
  s_ready_for_complete --> s_completed : Complete Checkout succeeds synchronously
  s_ready_for_complete --> s_complete_in_progress : Complete Checkout accepted for asynchronous processing
  s_ready_for_complete --> s_incomplete : Complete returns a recoverable change (for example payment_failed or out_of_stock)
  s_ready_for_complete --> s_requires_escalation : Complete returns a buyer handoff (requires_buyer_input or requires_buyer_review)
  s_complete_in_progress --> s_completed : Business finishes processing, any Action resolved
  s_incomplete --> s_canceled : Platform cancels, or the session expires
  s_requires_escalation --> s_canceled : Platform cancels, or the session expires
  s_ready_for_complete --> s_canceled : Platform cancels, or the session expires
  s_complete_in_progress --> s_canceled : Session invalid or expired (cancellation race rules apply)
  s_completed --> [*]
  s_canceled --> [*]
